phoenix: enable USB-C dual-role + PD sink PDOs (5V fixed, 5-9V variable) on pm6150_typec

Upstream v7.1_rc3 already adds the pm6150_charger node, ADC input
channels, and the qcom,pm6150-charger fallback compatible. What remains
is the Type-C connector role configuration: phoenix supports sink
operation (charging) in addition to source, with a 5V/3A fixed PDO plus
a 5-9V/3A variable PDO and a 27W operating sink power.

The 5-9V range lets the TCPM policy engine negotiate fixed 9V source
PDOs with modern PD wall chargers, matching the stock 9V/3A (27W)
fast-charge capability. This is only safe now that the charger driver
follows the negotiated voltage (0024 reprograms DCDC_FSW_SEL and
USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_CFG on every contract change); advertising >5V
before that made the PM6150 latch PAUSE_CHARGE via USBIN_OV and wall
charging never started (measured on-device). The range is deliberately
capped at 9V to stay within the stock fast-charge envelope; higher
source PDOs fall outside the advertised range and are rejected. No
APDO is advertised so PPS contracts are never selected.

Signed-off-by: phoenix port <fix@me>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -601,12 +601,17 @@
 	connector {
 		compatible = "usb-c-connector";
 
-		power-role = "source";
+		power-role = "dual";
 		data-role = "dual";
+		try-power-role = "sink";
 		self-powered;
 
 		source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
 			       PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM | PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
+		sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
+			     PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM | PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)
+			     PDO_VAR(5000, 9000, 3000)>;
+		op-sink-microwatt = <27000000>;
 
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
